# Repository instructions

## Layout

- Laboratory configuration: `opensdl.yaml`
- Workflows: `workflows/`
- Organization code: `src/{{ package }}/`
- Local adapters: `src/{{ package }}/adapters/`
- Organization domain models: `src/{{ package }}/domain/`
- Shared laboratory context: `docs/lab/`
- Tests: `tests/`

## Checks

- `uv run opensdl validate opensdl.yaml --workflow workflows/first-run.yaml`
- `uv run pytest`
- `uv run opensdl doctor --manifest opensdl.yaml` only when operational evidence is required;
  `doctor` initializes or updates the configured runtime store.

## Working state

- Use `start-here` to establish or update the laboratory context and first workflow. Use
  `orient-lab` for current declared status.
- Start fresh work with `git status --short`, the shared files under `docs/lab/`, and the selected
  manifest. Resume work by refreshing Git, tests, shared context, and the manifest.
- Query runtime evidence only when the task requires it, account for query side effects, and
  preserve unrelated changes and setup.
- Git records intended implementation and confirmed shared context. `.opensdl/` records local
  execution state and stays out of Git. Conversation history is private context.
- The active harness controls local permissions. The manifest, policy, and runtime control
  laboratory actions.

Repository skills live in `.agents/skills/`. Keep credentials, live endpoints, sensitive facility
details, and generated run state out of Git. Keep inventory claims separate from executable
configuration. Implement changes with tests and configuration.
